---
// Terms of Use. Mirrors the in-app Terms clause by clause, with the same
// numbering and wording (Paths repo,
// Paths/Views/SignUp/Onboarding/SignUpTermsContent.swift, lastUpdated
// "October 8, 2026"), including 15.1: deleting the account does not cancel a
// subscription bought through Apple. Change the two together.
//
// The party, the governing law and the contact address match the in-app text:
// Benjamin Jack Laubacher, the laws of Switzerland, support@particlesofmind.com.
// Two things differ on purpose: the date is the date this page went up, and
// clauses 8 and 19 link to /privacy and /terms rather than printing the URLs
// configured in the build.
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
---

<Layout title="Terms of Use" description="The terms for using Paths.">
  <LegalPage title="Terms of Use">
    <span slot="updated">8 November 2026</span>

    <h2 id="s1">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
    <p>
      By creating an account or using the Paths application ("App"), you agree to be bound by these Terms &amp;
      Conditions ("Terms"). If you do not agree to these Terms, do not create an account or use the App.
    </p>
    <p>
      These Terms constitute a legally binding agreement between you and Benjamin Jack Laubacher
      ("we," "us," or "our"). By tapping "Agree &amp; Continue" during sign-up, you confirm that you have read,
      understood, and accepted these Terms in full.
    </p>

    <h2 id="s2">2. Eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 16 years of age to use Paths; the App enforces this during sign-up. If you are under 18,
      you represent that your parent or legal guardian has reviewed and agreed to these Terms on your behalf.
    </p>
    <p>By using the App, you represent and warrant that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>You are at least 16 years old.</li>
      <li>You have the legal capacity to enter into this agreement.</li>
      <li>
        You are not located in a country subject to a U.S. government embargo or designated as a terrorist supporting
        country.
      </li>
      <li>You are not listed on any U.S. government list of prohibited or restricted parties.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="s3">3. Account Registration</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>3.1 Sign-In Methods.</strong> Paths supports sign-in via Apple ID and email/password. You are responsible
      for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and for all activity that occurs under your
      account.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>3.2 Accurate Information.</strong> You agree to provide accurate, current, and complete information during
      registration, including your name and age. You agree to keep this information up to date.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>3.3 One Account Per Person.</strong> Each account is for a single individual. You may not create multiple
      accounts or transfer your account to another person.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>3.4 Account Security.</strong> You agree to notify us immediately of any unauthorized use of your account.
      We are not liable for any loss resulting from unauthorized access to your account.
    </p>

    <h2 id="s4">4. Subscriptions and Billing</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>4.1 Subscription Plans.</strong> Paths offers two auto-renewing subscription tiers, Plus and Max, each
      available on a monthly or annual basis. Current prices for your region are shown in the App before purchase and
      in the App Store listing; they are not restated here.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>4.2 Billing.</strong> All subscriptions are processed through Apple's App Store and are subject to Apple's
      payment terms. Payment is charged to your Apple ID account at confirmation of purchase. Subscriptions
      automatically renew unless auto-renewal is turned off at least 24 hours before the end of the current period.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>4.3 Renewals.</strong> Your account will be charged for renewal within 24 hours prior to the end of the
      current subscription period. The renewal price will be the same as the original purchase price unless we notify
      you otherwise.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>4.4 Cancellations.</strong> You may cancel your subscription at any time through your Apple ID account
      settings. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period. We do not provide refunds for
      unused portions of a subscription period, except as required by applicable law or Apple's refund policies.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>4.5 Refunds.</strong> All refund requests are handled by Apple. To request a refund, visit
      <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>. We have no ability to issue refunds
      directly.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>4.6 Free Access.</strong> We reserve the right to offer free trials or a free tier at our discretion.
      Free access may be limited in features and is subject to change.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>4.7 Price Changes.</strong> We may change subscription prices at any time with reasonable notice.
      Continued use of the App after a price change takes effect constitutes your acceptance of the new price.
    </p>

    <h2 id="s5">5. User Content</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>5.1 Definition.</strong> User Content means any content you submit, upload, or share through the App,
      including but not limited to photographs submitted as proof of habit completion, GPS location data, audio
      recordings, profile information, group messages, and any other data you provide.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>5.2 Your Ownership.</strong> You retain ownership of User Content you create. By submitting User Content,
      you grant us a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free, sublicensable, and transferable license to use, store,
      display, and distribute your User Content solely for the purposes of operating and improving the App.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>5.3 Proof of Completion.</strong> Paths requires verifiable proof for certain habit completions, which may
      include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Photographs: images captured or selected from your library.</li>
      <li>GPS location data: geographic coordinates confirming you were at a specified location.</li>
      <li>Timed audio recordings: audio captured during a specified duration.</li>
      <li>
        Pose detection data: analysis of body position using your device's camera via Apple's Vision framework. Pose
        data is processed on-device and is not transmitted to our servers in raw form.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      By enabling these verification methods, you consent to the App accessing your device's camera, microphone, and
      location services as needed to verify completion. You can manage these permissions in your device settings at
      any time.
    </p>
    <p><strong>5.4 Content Standards.</strong> You agree not to submit User Content that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Is false, misleading, or fraudulent, including falsified proof of completion.</li>
      <li>Infringes any third-party intellectual property rights.</li>
      <li>Is obscene, defamatory, threatening, or harassing.</li>
      <li>Contains malware, viruses, or harmful code.</li>
      <li>Violates any applicable law or regulation.</li>
      <li>Depicts minors in any inappropriate context.</li>
      <li>Violates the privacy of any third party.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>5.5 Content Removal.</strong> We reserve the right to remove any User Content that violates these Terms or
      that we determine, in our sole discretion, is harmful, offensive, or otherwise objectionable.
    </p>

    <h2 id="s6">6. Social Features and Community Conduct</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>6.1 Groups.</strong> Paths allows users to join archetype-specific groups. Group membership is limited to
      one group per user account. Group participation is governed by the conduct standards in Section 5.4 and the
      additional rules below.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>6.2 Leaderboards.</strong> Participation in group leaderboards is pseudonymous, using your archetype and a
      short identifier. Real names are not displayed on public leaderboards unless you choose to disclose them.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>6.3 Social Feed.</strong> Verified habit completions may be shared to a social feed visible to other
      users. By completing a habit with social sharing enabled, you consent to that completion, including any
      associated proof content, being visible to other users within the App.
    </p>
    <p><strong>6.4 Prohibited Conduct.</strong> You agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Harass, bully, or threaten other users.</li>
      <li>Submit fraudulent or manipulated proof of completion.</li>
      <li>Attempt to gain unfair advantage in scoring or leaderboards.</li>
      <li>Solicit personal information from other users.</li>
      <li>Impersonate any person or entity.</li>
      <li>Use the social features for spam, advertising, or commercial solicitation.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>6.5 Reporting.</strong> If you encounter content or conduct that violates these Terms, please report it
      through the in-app reporting mechanism. We will investigate and take appropriate action.
    </p>

    <h2 id="s7">7. Arete (AI Assistant)</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>7.1 AI-Generated Content.</strong> Paths includes Arete, an AI-powered assistant that provides habit
      guidance, learning content, and interactive exercises. Arete's responses are generated by third-party large
      language models and are provided for informational and motivational purposes only.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>7.2 Not Professional Advice.</strong> Arete's responses do not constitute medical, psychological, fitness,
      nutritional, financial, or any other form of professional advice. Do not rely on Arete as a substitute for
      qualified professional guidance. Always consult a qualified professional before making decisions that affect your
      health, wellbeing, or finances.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>7.3 Accuracy.</strong> AI-generated responses may contain inaccuracies, errors, or outdated information.
      We make no warranty regarding the accuracy, completeness, or fitness for purpose of any AI-generated content.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>7.4 Your Inputs.</strong> Conversations with Arete may be transmitted through our AI proxy and processed
      by third-party AI providers to generate responses. Do not share sensitive personal information, such as financial
      details, government ID numbers, or medical records, with Arete.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>7.5 Third-Party AI Providers.</strong> Arete is powered by third-party AI infrastructure. Your use of Arete
      is also subject to the terms and privacy policies of those providers.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>7.6 Retention and Safety.</strong> We may retain prompts, responses, and operational metadata for abuse
      prevention, service reliability, and quality improvement, as described in our Privacy Policy.
    </p>

